      "description": "Watch Talleres Cordoba vs Velez Sarsfield highlights and goals from Argentine Primera División on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 31, 2026. The Liga Profesional Argentina clash between Talleres de Cordoba and Velez Sarsfield on July 31, 2026, delivered a tactical battle filled with intensity. Fans witnessed a game where defensive discipline was tested against clinical finishing, keeping the result in doubt until the very final moments. A Tightly Contested Opening Half Talleres de Cordoba started the match with intent, looking to use their home advantage to unsettle the visitors. Their persistence paid off in the 27th minute when Ronaldo Martinez found the back of the net, clinical in his finish after being set up by Timoteo Chamorro . Velez Sarsfield struggled with discipline shortly after, as Matias Pellegrini and Federico Fattori both picked up yellow cards. However, the visitors found a way back just before the whistle; in the 45th minute, Rodrigo Aliendro equalized following an assist from Elias Gomez , ensuring the sides went into the break level at 1-1. Tactical Shifts and Second Half Drama The second half saw a series of substitutions as both managers looked for a decisive edge. The momentum shifted in favor of Velez Sarsfield following the introduction of Lucas Robertone . In the 79th minute, Robertone turned provider for Thiago Silvero , who struck home to give the visitors the lead. Talleres attempted to respond by bringing on fresh legs like Bruno Barticciotto , but they found it difficult to break down a resilient Velez backline. As the clock struck 90 minutes, Velez Sarsfield put the game beyond reach. Diego Valdes , a late substitute for Luca Feler , converted a pass from Thiago Aguirre to make it 3-1. A late yellow card for Valentin Fascendini in stoppage time reflected the frustration of the home side as Velez Sarsfield celebrated a hard-fought away victory."
